# Grandfathered cross-package references: files under packages/*/lib that name
# a module (call, capture, apply/3, `@compile no_warn_undefined`, `use`,
# typespec, atom, or a module/process name used as a value) living in a tree
# the package's mix.exs does not declare for :prod.
# One `file<TAB>module<TAB>owning tree` per line; `undefined` means no
# defmodule in the repo matches. Checked by scripts/check_package_boundaries.exs.
#
# This list only shrinks: CI fails on an entry the pull request's base does
# not have. Entries are not a licence to use the module: each one breaks when
# the package runs without that tree. Remove an entry when the site is fixed
# (module moved into the owning package, implementation injected via
# application config, or reference deleted).
